OpenPolaris
Copyright 2026 Ian Morgan and OpenPolaris contributors

This product includes software developed as part of the
benro-polaris-firmware-patcher project
(https://github.com/ian-morgan99/benro-polaris-firmware-patcher).

The OpenPolaris Kotlin/Compose client was originally developed on
the `agents/benro-polaris-firmware-analysis` branch of that project
(2026-08-26), under the MIT License as listed in that branch's
`polaris-client/README.md`.  OpenPolaris continues under the same
MIT terms.  See `docs/FIRMWARE-ANALYSIS-ALPACA.md` for the
firmware ground-truth analysis that informed the protocol
implementation.

The "Benro Polaris" name is used only to identify hardware
compatibility.  OpenPolaris is an independent, community project
and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or produced by Benro.

Bundled astronomical data (catalog.json, stars.json, ngc.json,
comets.json) is sourced from public-domain catalogues.  See
docs/THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md for the per-shard source attribution,
licence, and regeneration guidance.  In summary:

  - Messier (1781): public domain
  - NGC 2000.0 (Sinnott 1988, NASA): public domain
  - Yale Bright Star Catalogue 5th Ed. (Hoffleit & Warren 1991):
    public domain
  - Hipparcos Input Catalogue (ESA, 1997): public domain
  - JPL Small-Body Database (JPL / Caltech, US govt work): public domain
